 {:db/id "q-105039" :question/id #uuid "91d09261-286a-5e85-a61f-8483207f7bbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105039" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only ${Z}^{-}⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every negative integer is a natural number. For example, we have $-1\\in {Z}^{-}$ but $-1\\notin N.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105039/ma-source-field/e42ea873ee538626cf850e7133110248a47f3f135a3835302534254c83faeec0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
