 {:db/id "q-105880" :question/id #uuid "e54b8763-b5a0-5c43-83dd-f8cff2d18e0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105880" :question/problem "If $A={1,2,3,4,5,6,7}$, which collection of subsets of $A$ is a partition of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{1,2,3,4,5},{6,7}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{1,2,3,4,5},{6,7}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{1,2,3,4},{5},{6,7,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $8$ does not appear in $A.$\n\n- ${{1,2,3,4,5,6},{6,7}}$ is not a partition because the element $6$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{2,3,4,5,6,7}}$ is not a partition because the element $1\\in A$ does not appear in any subset." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105880/ma-source-field/56c58bc83276919a551306138f0726e6b8e16306ebacf97b55211dedd89da71d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
