 {:db/id "q-105883" :question/id #uuid "f8c8b7d8-3302-5432-860d-76a8d6e3c60a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105883" :question/problem "If $S={0,1,2,3,4,5}$, which collection of subsets of $S$ is a partition of $S?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $S$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $S$ where every element of $S$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,2,4},{1,3,5}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{0,2,4},{1,3,5}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,3,4,5,6}}$ is not a partition because the element $6$ does not appear in $S.$\n\n- ${{0,1},{2},{4,5}}$ is not a partition because the element $3\\in S$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{0,1},{1,2,3,4,5}}$ is not a partition because the element $1$ appears in two subsets." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105883/ma-source-field/adb8aa29712ebf1882bf1d2c204016f6512b2ac8f3f53a71648acb74166c3ffc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
