 {:db/id "q-105973" :question/id #uuid "e0a49cc3-1c47-5fec-b0e3-f57e7984dec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105973" :question/problem "If $Y={0,2,4,…,140},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,4,8,…,140},{2,6,10,…,138}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{0,4,8,…,140},{2,10,18,…,138}}$  is not a partition because some elements of $Y$ (such as $6)$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{0,4,8,…,140},{2,4,6,…,138}}$ is not a partition because the elements $4,8,…,140$ appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,140}}$ is not a partition because the element $0\\in Y$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${∅,{0,2,4,…,140}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105973/ma-source-field/0c6a4af91cd107fa9586147bd8f74145bc3a0c2c62bbd37da3346ddf0d634136"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
