 {:db/id "q-105976" :question/id #uuid "2c08f743-5eb8-541e-99bf-bb3b4d7c20f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105976" :question/problem "If $A={0,10,20,…,900},$ which collection of subsets of $A$ is a partition of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0},{10,20,30,…,900}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{0,10,20,…,900}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{10,30,50…,890},{20,40,60,…,900}}$ is not a partition because the element $0$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{0,10,20,…,890}},{20,40,60,…,900}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $20,40,60,…,900,$ that appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- ${{10,30,50…,890}},{0,20,40,60,…,800}}$ is not a partition because the elements $820,840…,900$ do not appear in any subsets." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105976/ma-source-field/4e4eb9f4219e231c0ac97004119a89b56f11de7ba27814654a1fe1deaf3b4edf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
