 {:db/id "q-106654" :question/id #uuid "6f61f141-3dc0-53a6-8909-845a088a0525" :question/math-academy-id "q-106654" :question/problem "Given that $y>30$ and $t>0,$ which of the following is an inhibited decay equation?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited decay equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-k(y-a),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $y>a$ for all $t>0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited decay equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=840-28y.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-28(y-30).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=28,$ and $a=30.$ Note that for inhibited decay, we must have $y>30$ for all $t>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106654/ma-source-field/c7fdb1069508e21c25c5580733f1bd52aed8329576bce6afe894f4113f736e2b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
