 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "092a8c01-7fc1-532c-ba20-9cb4c823a717"] :question/problem "Given that $y<80$ and $t\\ge 0,$ which of the following is an inhibited growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=400-5y.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=5(80-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=5,$ and $a=80.$ Note that for inhibited growth, we must have $y<80$ for all $t\\ge 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106662/ma-source-field/3ec596c83ee9cef94dd51b18451dc6080cd65db6305e1d53e0bda10113ed803d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
