 {:db/id "q-106865" :question/id #uuid "ac90b5bc-97a8-5910-8e4c-691ef1d83be3" :question/math-academy-id "q-106865" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${R}_{15}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $15?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{15}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{15}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{15}[t])=15+1=16.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106865/ma-source-field/41195cde072063948d51b7551a05db8c6263b2f773f6fb8c5c4751b464b9a799"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
