 {:db/id "q-106866" :question/id #uuid "125dfbaf-7832-535b-889e-b97a19233f9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106866" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${R}_{20}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $20?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{20}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{20}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{20}[t])=20+1=21.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106866/ma-source-field/2dc3a614f51128a8a4e116355bf5df9aaec79984e4db02c1a5c225e59c735684"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
