 {:db/id "q-106888" :question/id #uuid "90418efb-5f81-5124-80f6-ce7467b7ec0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106888" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ the vector space of all $8\\times 8$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{8}(R))={8}^{2}=64.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106888/ma-source-field/889a79523939f8ab8b3b47ab9914327299a259f57915e3d3cbf00d8ec2671de1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
