 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ba1ee846-cfe9-595c-9803-25afded75ec1"] :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
