 {:db/id "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79" :answer-field/id #uuid "efb92f1c-9bb7-5cc3-9d68-87a83b156926" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/8a236e501d52126cb889385f0d30f7b4cbfdb66163cbe8f1955e21cb3c620bed" "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/9909387cad715efd84810cbc3093a5f44d425ad2b050b39fa080445b6dbde394" "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/d5ee214fc4ebdb964d67239e3da5811b7c787bb4ef47ec0ccbaa764f05d5fe99" "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/7a14e161b9701c2c1678a00df7b4ce39522df64ffff663ec5c1c7f84264bf6b6" "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/7697b742b99d3fcc3812743ec3e07f8fd8e673d6fe459880d276020f3ffa1217"] :answer-field/correct "q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79/7697b742b99d3fcc3812743ec3e07f8fd8e673d6fe459880d276020f3ffa1217" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-109695" :question/id #uuid "0737f5ff-3d66-5f51-b7b8-b8bf8fe97f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-109695" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}+5{y}^{″}-3{t}^{2}{y}^{′}=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & a & c\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-5{y}^{″}+3{t}^{2}{y}^{′}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-5{x}_{3}+3{t}^{2}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=3{t}^{2}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3{t}^{2} & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $a=3{t}^{2},b=1,c=-5,$ and $a+b+c=3{t}^{2}-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109695/ma-source-field/d7bb4c829f43ac00f9bcf6f955f5be5da537085ef2904ea7bfd99e141b640a79"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
