 {:db/id "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f937f66-6317-5bbf-a1a5-7a91aa314279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/c8dcb040ad8b506ab0ab3f6149a7a1fc6bc9fc892de5ef5e812ff26eca47bae4" "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/2f1fcb0f74e5c0b0383931f08da2a71b069e6c3dace13a42c7b0cd5f2e064720" "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/22aed67ae888abdcf739f0888fe0226dcd4684ec46a80cd1bd2b893c1a986eb4" "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/3ba40cb1ae39a894b7b3ed5881d87be06c1725042837ee017674402a08660a2c"] :answer-field/correct "q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5/c8dcb040ad8b506ab0ab3f6149a7a1fc6bc9fc892de5ef5e812ff26eca47bae4" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-109865" :question/id #uuid "3b884b20-b24f-567b-b7d3-aeaaf2084dca" :question/math-academy-id "q-109865" :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ under the action of $A+B?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A+B$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A+B:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (a+b)_{1} & (a+b)_{2} & ⋯ & (a+b)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A+B}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A+B$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B),$ the column space of $A+B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/02/02a739d8888f2b46b81075218693e6b2cc87e3c5b81b522abfc9246dcd7c870d.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109865/ma-source-field/9bfe674732f236f001a5e86c86fc52af20550f69e61e3e79e1eb63aaacef61d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
