 {:db/id "q-111311" :question/id #uuid "d551bbb5-65f5-5733-b15c-2c116cdaa662" :question/math-academy-id "q-111311" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=5-{X}^{3}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $a$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $b$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=5-{X}^{3}$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.55$ | $0.25$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $c=0.2,$ and $a+c=6.2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111311/ma-source-field/cebf37f2a98deda14c8399346e19ef6ccd2d3dbfd0772b4d3182e3e335f12800"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
