 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "b2568364-334f-50f4-8bf6-71938e74b4ef"] :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\nLet $Y={X}^{4}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $b$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $0.2$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+d?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y={X}^{4}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $16$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,1,16}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for both $Y=1$ and $Y=16.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.2 \\\\ P(Y=1) & =0.1+0.1 \\\\ P(Y=16) & =0.1+0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=1,b=16,d=0.6,$ and $a+b+d=17.6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111314/ma-source-field/4a415036ebeadf6e53a73969d74fb5923ae201797530ddb9f9cc3529121a272a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
