 {:db/id "q-111330" :question/id #uuid "694fef37-1166-5153-b6b0-893dc9dcd03f" :question/math-academy-id "q-111330" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=16-{X}^{2}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.35$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=16-{X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $15$ | $16$ | $15$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,15,16}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for $Y=15.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.35 \\\\ P(Y=15) & =0.15+0.2 \\\\ P(Y=16) & =0.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $15$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.35$ | $0.35$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=15,c=0.35,$ and $a+c=15.35.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
